{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/355787-ghostbusters-inc","id":355787,"title":"Ghostbusters, Inc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-31T09:06:58-08:00","id":355787,"title":"Ghostbusters, Inc.","content":"So after re-watching first film for it's 30th anniversary with my partner, I thought: &quot;Hell, Ghostbusters <b>are</b> a Hunter cell! Maybe even Compact?&quot; - So for this is topic: <b>How would you put a Ghostbusters, Inc. in World of Darkness?</b><br /> <br /> Obviously they hunt for both materialized ghosts <b>and</b> spirits, as some beings, like <a href=\"http://ghostbusters.wikia.com/wiki/Slimer\" target=\"_blank\">Slimer</a> or <a href=\"http://ghostbusters.wikia.com/wiki/Zuul\" target=\"_blank\">Zuul</a>, are better as &quot;dark animism&quot; ephemera than dead ones. They have Endowments - they own build equipment - but they are small in man power. Last big question is that: <b>How could they work as company in world were people do not belive in supernatural and even activey forget about it?</b> No one would pay them for their work...<br /> <br /> And a small treat for the fans <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/Fe93CLbHjxQ\" data-code=\"Fe93CLbHjxQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Fe93CLbHjxQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-31-2014, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:27:27-08:00","id":355908,"title":"","content":"You are a new and upcoming firm, you\u00b4re having silly commercials in late night airtime on minor channels, a flashy logo and homepage.<br /> You\u00b4re daily business is going to afternoon talkshows, writing spiritual self-help books and selling blinking devices that are supposed to optimize<br /> the Chi-Flow in houses of gullible old people.<br /> You\u00b4re real business interest, albeit less profitable at the time is dealing with ethereal manifestations.<br /> You work scientifically: You observe, you test, you get results. You have identified and categorized a wide range of spirits and ghosts and developed <br /> the proper tools to ban or catch them. Some day there will be a dissertion, a patent and billions of dollars. Right now it\u00b4s getting rid of the Poltergeist in<br /> Gramma\u00b4s cellar. <br /> <br /> Suggestion:<br /> Go Nerdcore: You\u00b4re the cast of Big Bang Theory thrown into the abyss of the WoD. Your brains and equipment keeps you alive.<br /> Have Night Vision Goggles, Army wear, riot vehicles everthing that\u00b4s &quot;kewl&quot;. Go through the glossary of the WoD and get rid of the spiritiual gibberish.<br /> Then add scientific gibberish : Third categoric semi-transperant levitating apparition, of clearly hostile nature.<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> Are you dealing with Ghosts exclusively ? Do your characters count Spirits as Ghosts? Slimer could be a spirit of gluttony.<br /> Do you &quot;kill&quot; ghosts ? Ban them? Catch them &quot;alive&quot;? Could be a moral issue in that ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T12:03:12-08:00","id":355934,"title":"","content":"Ghostbusters in the WoD:<br /> <br /> Depending on how much you allow other Splats into the game you could tread on many toes:<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero:</b> They\u00b4re actually like you. Maybe some or all of you were NWZ until they decided to get paid for it.<br /> <b>Cheiron Group:</b> You\u00b4re reputation as charlatans kept them off so far. But someday some corporate asshole with a money bag might want to buy you out.<br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey</b>: Some high-class sociopath bought an original 16th century rifle with magic sigils and silver bullets for his first hunt and you stole his shot.<br /> <b>Sin Eaters</b> Clear case of stepping in someone else\u00b4s turf. Also they are are heavily inflicted with a semi-hominid mind-controlling creature. Untrustworthy.<br /> <b>Vampires and Werewolves</b> If you want to cage thousands of ghosts in a container, that might produce a Wound, a Locus, a Dragon\u00b4s Nest...<br /> Prepare for special interest groups knocking down your door.<br /> <b>Mages</b> Some might want you to be silenced. Some might want you to go public. There is an espionage/counter-espionage battle of which you are ignorant<br /> <br /> Also have fun with other creatures if they want to negotiate.<br /> Watch some Atheist convention speeches and apply that to their beliefs. No, &quot;the spirits told me&quot; is not sufficient proof.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1261,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","user":"Doc Lumbago","date":". 12-31-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T15:27:33-08:00","id":356055,"title":"","content":"It's not for Hunter, but Saturnine Night for the Promethean line deals extensively with bringing fringe science (or more accurately &quot;weird&quot; science) into your WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T16:38:41-08:00","id":356096,"title":"","content":"You know, it surprises me that nobody tried to create a ghost-busters hunter group before. As a group they work mostly at compact level. As for the formation of the group itself I would consider them a faction of Null mysteries or a splinter group. In fact the ghost-busters is what you have when you take a group of guys from network zero, null mysteries and the loyalists of thule with an interest for ghosts and put them together. Their endowments can be copied from taskforce valkyrie since is mostly supertech, only repurposed for ghots and spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T16:55:21-08:00","id":356103,"title":"","content":"here's something from my files<br /> <br /> <b>The Ghostbusters</b><br /> This write up of the Ghostbusters is based on the first two films, as well as parts from the Real Ghostbusters animated series (and the Ghostbusters RPG by West End Games).<br /> <br /> <b>Egon Spengler</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Faith; Egon had an unshakable belief that even supernatural events could be explained in a scientific context.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Gluttony; Egon is actively addicted to the scientific exploration of paranormal events, and will take any opportunity to conduct a proper scientific investigation (even when socially inappropriate).<br /> Egon would also have the flaw of Behavior Blind.<br /> <br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits of Note: </b>Eidetic Memory, Fame 1, FS: Combat Marksmanship 1, Professional Training 5 (Scientist), Quick Draw (Firearms), Technophile<br /> <br /> <b>Skills of Note: </b> Academics 3(History), Athletics 1 (Climbing), Computers 3, Crafts 4 (Ghost busting), Firearms 2 (Proton Pack), Investigation 3 (Research), Occult 3(Ephemeral Entities), Science 5 (Physics), Subterfuge 2(Disguise)<br /> <br /> <b>Ray Stantz </b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Hope; Ray is the heart of the Ghostbusters, and has a sincere desire to help humanity <br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust; Ray\u2019s enthusiasm gets him into trouble; and he often leaps before he looks or speaks before thinking about what he is about to say<br /> <br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits of Note: </b>Encyclopedic Knowledge, Fame 1, FS: Combat Marksmanship 1, Professional Training 4(Scientist), Quick Draw (Firearms)<br /> <br /> <b>Skills of Note: </b> Academics 3(Religion), Athletics 2(Throwing), Computers 2, Crafts 3 (Ghost busting), Drive 1(Pilot), Empathy 2, Firearms 2 (Proton Pack), Investigation 3 (Occult), Occult 4, Science 4 (Parapsychology)<br /> <br /> <b>Peter Venkman </b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Justice; Peter is a stand up guy, and who looked out for the little guy, tried to sincerely help people, and took an instant dislike to bullies, petty bureaucrats and power-tripping demi-gods.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust; while Peter seemed to indulge in several vices (Greed and Lust foremost); He seemed to go out of his way (and perform questionable actions) to gain the attention of attractive women. <br /> <br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> Presence 3, Manipulation 3 Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits of Note: </b>Barfly, FS: Combat Marksmanship 1, Fame 1, Professional Training 3 (Academic), Quick Draw (Firearms)<br /> <br /> <b>Skills of Note: </b> Academics 3(Psychology), Athletics 2, Brawl 1(Sucker Punch), Computers 2, Expression 3 (Rant), Firearms 2 (Proton Pack), Investigation 2, Occult 2, Persuasion 3(Seduction), Politics 2(Academic, Bureaucracy), Science 2 (Parapsychology), Socialize 2, Subterfuge 3 (Lies), Streetwise 3 (New York)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Winston Zeddemore </b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Temperance; Winston was a down to earth blue color guy who help moderate the more extreme personalities of the other Ghostbusters.<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Greed; Winston was willing to adopt a strange and dangerous profession for few reason other than steady pay.<br /> <br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits of Note:</b> Common Sense, Fame 1, FS: Boxing 1, FS: Combat Marksmanship 2, HP Driving 2, Professional Training 3 (Laborer), Quick Draw (Firearms), Strong Back, Wheelman<br /> <br /> <b>Skills of Note: </b> Academics 1(Religion), Athletics 3(Climbing, Throwing), Brawl 2 (Grapple), Crafts 2 (Repair), Drive 3, Empathy 1, Firearms 3(Proton Pack), Intimidation 3, Investigation 1,Occult 1(Layman\u2019s Terms), Persuasion 2, Science 1(Layman\u2019s Terms), Socialize 2 (Down to Earth), Streetwise 2 (New York), Weaponry 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>Tactics: </b>The Ghostbusters may use Tactics (Hunter: The Vigil). The most often employ the following; Corral<b>, </b>Exorcism<b>, </b>Measurements and Net.<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment: </b>The Ghostbusters\u2019s make use of an arsenal of advanced weapons and equipment.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Containment Grid (Size 10, Durability 5) </i></b><br /> The Containment Grid stores all the ghost and spirits that the Ghostbusters capture. It can hold potentially hundreds, if not thousands of entities. An entity imprisoned in the Containment Grid is in a state of slumber, and will remain so unless the Grid is compromised. If the Grid is damaged or powered down, the contained spirits immediately awaken and escape.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ecto-1 </i></b><br /> Ecto-1 is a modified Cadillac Miller-Meteor Ambulance that serves as the Ghostbusters primary transport. It is heavily outfitted with weapons racks, sensory equipment, lights, and its distinctive siren. The vehicle stores 4 sets of Proton Packs, 6 PKE Meters, Ghost Traps and Ecto Visors, and an assortment of mundane equipment (tools, flashlights, climbing gears, communication devices, etc)<br /> Durability: 3, Size: 16, Structure: 19, Acceleration: 13, Safe Speed: 99, Speed: 192, Handling: 2, Occupants: 1+ 4<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ecto-Visors (Size 1, Durability 1) </i></b><br /> These modified Night vision Goggles have the added benefit of being able to detect and perceive ephemeral entities are manifested or in Twilight, but would otherwise be imperceptible.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ectoplasm-Blower (Size 4, Durability 3) </i></b><br /> These devices project a stream of psychomagnetherically charged ectoplasm (a.k.a mood slime) over a wide area. This weapon is used infrequently as it requires vast amount of difficult to obtain ectoplasm. The ectoplasm is charged with a strong positive resonance, and targets struck by it must make a Resolve +Composure (at a -3 penalty) roll or be overwhelmed by positive sensations, and suffer a -3 penalty to dice polls for any hostile action for the remainder of the scene. Entities with a low morality (3 or less) or associated with negative concepts that are materialized or possessing a mortal are not effected by the mood altering effects of the slime, but lose 1 point of essence for each success on the attack roll. Resolve attacks with this weapon as long burst of autofire.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ghost Trap (Size 2, Durability 2) </i></b><br /> This trap is a sturdy box with a hinged lid and tethered to a cable (usually 3-5 yards) with a foot pedal at the end. Pressing the lever opens the box, which generates a force field capable of drawing in and trapping ghost and spirits. Ghost Traps may be positioned, or treated as a thrown weapon. When opened, the trap units a brilliant white cone of energy that draws in any nearby ephemeral entities (manifested, materialized, or in Twilight). Once triggered, any Spirit within 3 yards of the Trap must make roll with their Power with a penalty of -5. If successful, the Spirit evades capture. Otherwise, they are drawn into the trap and cannot escape until the trap is opened or destroyed. A single trap may hold up to 3 discreet entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Jump Suit:</b> The Ghostbusters signature Jumpsuit\u2019s are fire retardant and provide Armor 1/0.<br /> <br /> <b><i>PKE Meter (Size 1, Durability 1) </i></b><br /> PKE (Psychokinetic Energy) Meters are hand held devices that detect Ephemeral Entities. The device has a light display and arms that raise and lower based on the power and proximity of ghost and Spirits in Twilight. Reading the Meter is an Extended Intelligence +Science or Wits +Composure roll.<br /> Every 3 successes reveals a detail; Number of Entities (Single, Multiple (2 or more), Many (10+), Horde (20+)), Power (Based on Entities Rank +Highest Trait Score (Low (1-4), Moderate (5-8), High (9-12), Extreme (13+), and Proximity (Close (Less than 10 meters), Medium (11-30 meters), Far (31-60 meters). Other creature with an Essence score (Ridden, Hosts, and Werewolves) can also be detected, but at a -3 die penalty.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Proton Pack (Size 4, Durability 3) </i></b><br /> These small charged particle accelerators fire a stream of energy capable of injuring or subduing ephemeral entities. Attacks with the Proton Pack are made with Dexterity +Firearms. The weapon has two major settings;<br /> <i>Disruption:</i> The basic setting allows lethal damage to be dealt to manifested or materialized ephemeral entities. The erratic path of the beam allows targets to use their defense against the attack. The beams are less effective against non-ephemeral targets, and only deal bashing damage against them (unless an exceptional success is scored, which converts the damage to lethal).<br /> <i>Containment:</i> The Contain setting allows a Spirit to be grappled at a range. The Spirit must be within its last 3 health boxes for this setting to be effective. The target may apply their defense but is considered Immobilized on a successful attack. Spirits attempting to escape must make a Power roll with a -3 penalty, and achieve more successes than were scored on the initial Containment attack. A Spirit that has been contained may be moved a distance of 3 yards/per success on a (Strength +Athletics) roll. <br /> Crossing the Streams is Bad. It only happens if it done intentionally, or if two or more Ghostbusters attacking the same target in the same turn suffers Dramatic failures. What results is a catastrophic explosion that deals Force 6L (9-again, Knockdown) damage with a blast area of 20 yards. Any ephemeral entities in the area take aggravated damage instead of lethal, and any gateways into the Hisil or other plane of existence are immediately closed.<br /> Damage 3(L), Range 15/30/45, Strength: 3, Size: 4<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T23:43:08-08:00","id":356339,"title":"","content":"Did not play Ghostbusers Videogme, but buyed three days on Steam sale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My partner was watching our Polish Youtube game reviewer ( <b>Quaz</b> ) and for him it's &quot;Ghostbusters part three, never done&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So I would count the game as good canon material. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/NQqwzEyST8E\" data-code=\"NQqwzEyST8E\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NQqwzEyST8E/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> With <b>Reighnhell</b> post ( thank you man, very much! ) we solve almost all problems of topic. Beside one: <b>How can Ghostbusters Inc. work in World of Darkness were humanity forgets about supernatural after encounter? </b>They need to get income, as private company. But clients would not pay them, as they would be under the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you/\" target=\"_blank\">Lie</a> effect of universum.<br /> <br /> As side note, when I would do 2ed convesion of <b>Reighnhell</b> materials, I would only change a bit Virtues and Vices of guys. <i>Egon</i> would have a Virtue of Rationalist ( but still connected to general Faith ), <i>Ray</i> would get Vice of Curiosity ( still connected to more general Lust ), <i>Peter </i>could get additional Vices as Merits for him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And the info for fans - <i>Ghostbusters</i> reboot in production is to be <a href=\"http://spinoff.comicbookresources.com/2014/12/30/paul-feigs-ghostbusters-reboot-will-be-scarier-than-original/\" target=\"_blank\">more grim and spooky, and with all girls team</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More dark take on franchise could mean that new film will be more in tones of World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T10:18:44-08:00","id":356688,"title":"","content":"It's likely that in WoD the Ghostbusters would never become famous as they did in the movies, but rather might be considered something of a joke to most people... until they actually encounter a ghost or spirit and decide to quietly give these yahoos a shot after all. Skeptics and cynics might suspect or even accuse the group of manufacturing &quot;hauntings&quot; themselves to drum up business, but those in the know (occultists, supernatural beings and other hunters) probably notice that they do actually get results and seem to know what they're doing for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T15:11:19-08:00","id":357792,"title":"","content":"Check out <i>Orpheus</i>, from oWoD. It's about a corporation that hires astral projectors and mercenary ghosts to deal with supernatural problems, and is basically a proto-Conspiracy with a lot of good ideas. Very neat stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}